==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Kaijin Doge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*6 [[Madam Peng]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Emperor Warumongar]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*7 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*3 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[High Countess Koryessa]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
It is highly advised to boost [[Helmet Cat (Special Cat)|Yellow Nyanko Ranger]] to as high of a level as you can manage if you have no better options, since this stage is quite relentless. It swarms you with high-pressure enemies right off the bat. The best approach is to simply protect [[Giga-Nyan Rex (Uber Rare Cat)|Giga-Nyan Prime DX]] while it slowly handles the Shadow Boxer Ks and Madam Pengs. Most other attackers are usually too slow and, unless you're fighting right next to the Cat Base, won't be able to make it to the frontlines in time. Because of this, the best attackers for this stage are fast units that can quickly deal with peons, such as [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]. [[Goggles Cat (Special Cat)|Green Nyanko Ranger]] and [[Ribbon Cat (Special Cat)|Pink Nyanko Ranger]] are a given, helping stall out most threats ridiculously well. Mind your cash, as you want to have enough on hand to send out a second Giga-Nyan the moment it goes off cooldown.

Your win condition is to either get rid of Emperor Warumongar or kill all three Shadow Boxer Ks.

